FINAL ANSWER:
**Bus factor is 1: Troy Goode owns most of the surviving code.**

I used `git blame` on the 7 tracked JS files and counted the lines each author still owns. I skipped the formatting-only commit `62628c0`, which Fiona Formatter made on 2026-04-12. I also ignored whitespace changes and tracked moved lines. Without that, Fiona would show as owner of almost every line.

**Surviving lines (all 7 files)**

| Author | Lines | Share (approx.) | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 676 | about 55% | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 394 | about 32% | before May 2025 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 30 | 2–3% | not checked |
| Eric di Domenico | 16 | about 1% | not checked |
| Alberto Leal | 15 | about 1% | not checked |
| About 20 others | under 10 each | the rest | not checked |

I took the shares from the 12 authors listed above and didn't total every author, so treat the percentages as approximate.

**By file**
- `lib/index.js` is the core file. Troy owns 159 lines and Douglas 22. Alejandro owns 12, Raymond Feng 7 and max.laverse 6. Troy is the sole real owner.
- `test/test.js` is the largest test file. It is split between Douglas (339) and Troy (317), and it is the only file with real shared ownership.
- `test/error-response.js`, `test/example-app.js`, `test/issue-2.js` and `test/vary.js` are mostly or entirely Troy's. `test/vary.js` is 100% Troy.
- `test/support/env.js` is 2 lines, both Douglas's.

**Risks**
- Troy alone is more than 50% of the code. If Troy leaves, the core file has no knowledgeable maintainer.
- Troy's last commit was 2026-04-10, about 6 months before today (2026-10-22). That is past the skill's 90-day "active" threshold, so Troy counts as inactive.
- Douglas is the second owner, but I didn't see a recent commit from them. They don't appear among the 12 most recent committers, whose latest commit dates back to 2025-05-17. They look inactive too.
- The people committing recently (Ulises Gascón, Jon Church, Vansh Sharma and dependabot) own almost none of the surviving code. Recent activity and code ownership are different groups here.

**Limits**
- The count covers only 7 JS files, so the "by module" and dependents steps in the skill add little. Only `lib/index.js` has real dependents.
- Two "Troy Goode" git identities exist, with different emails. Blame merged them by name. If you want them separated, I'd need to check by email.
- I didn't use the contributor-analyzer agent. The blame data above answered the question directly.

**Recommendations**
1. Have someone active review `lib/index.js`, then take over `test/vary.js` and `test/error-response.js`.
2. Add a short doc on how the handler annotations in `lib/` work. Troy's latest commit (`b2005d9`) added them.
3. Add a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file listing `62628c0`. Then GitHub and local blame stop attributing the code to the formatting commit.

